Approach 3: Monotonic Stack ⭐ (Most Optimal)
Intuition

Maintain a Monotonic Decreasing Stack.

Instead of storing only prices,

store

(price, span)

Whenever the current price is greater than or equal to the stack top,

pop it and add its span.

This avoids recounting previous days.

Algorithm
Current Price

↓

Top <= Current

↓

Pop

↓

Add Span

↓

Push(Current Price, Span)

↓

Return Span

Java (Your Code)
class Node{
    int data;
    int count;

    Node(int data, int count){
        this.data = data;
        this.count = count;
    }
}

class StockSpanner {

    private Stack<Node> stack;

    public StockSpanner() {
        stack = new Stack<Node>();
    }

    public int next(int price) {

        int count = 1;

        while(!stack.isEmpty() && stack.peek().data <= price){

            Node node = stack.pop();

            count = count + node.count;
        }

        stack.push(new Node(price, count));

        return count;
    }
}

