Complexity Analysis
Approach	Idea	Time per next()	Space
Brute Force	Scan backwards	O(n)	O(n)
Better	Jump using stored spans	Worst O(n)	O(n)
Monotonic Stack	Store (price, span)	Amortized O(1)	O(n)
Why Amortized O(1)?

Each stock price is:

Pushed exactly once
Popped at most once

So for n calls:

Total Pushes = n

Total Pops = n

Total Operations = 2n

Average work per query:

O(1)
